    Name the accountable manual closure path and validate its artifact
    
    The Clerk found the independent-closure gate incomplete: the collector stopped
    automatic closure but nothing stated who may close a case or what evidence the
    case must carry. Closure is a recorded manual decision by the Clerk after
    inspecting an independent Judiciary disposition. Document that in the standing
    policy and the collector docstring, and mechanically require a case-bound
    closure_evidence object with a recognised disposition, verified_by=judiciary,
    an accountable verifier, a durable evidence_ref and recorded_by=clerk.
    
    This is a completeness check, not proof of truth: the collector never sets
    verified_closed and does not judge the disposition. The smoke test now shows a
    complete independent artifact accepted, while a self-declared Executive
    artifact stays listed as unresolved.

